  "completedSection": "Customer Satisfaction Monitoring Procedure: 1. **Data Sources**: Annual survey, post-project feedback forms, quarterly business review (QBR) meetings, on-time delivery (OTD) and quality (DPPM) metrics, customer complaints/SCARs, and win/loss analysis for quotes. 2. **Analysis Methodology**: Quantitative analysis (scores, trends, statistical significance), qualitative analysis (thematic coding of open-ended feedback), and root cause analysis for negative feedback. 3. **Action Triggers**: Overall score < 80%, any individual attribute score < 70%, negative trend over two periods, specific critical complaint, or loss of key business. Triggers a formal Corrective Action (CA) per ISO 9001:2015 clause 10.2. 4. **Frequency & Trending**: Surveys annually; QBRs, OTD, DPPM, complaints quarterly. All data trended quarterly and reviewed annually for long-term patterns. 5. **Communication of Results**: Results, trends, and actions summarized in monthly management review (clause 9.3). Key findings and improvements communicated to customers (e.g., in QBRs) and relevant internal departments. Annual summary reported to top management for strategic planning.",
  "references": "ISO 9001:2015 clauses 9.1.2 (Customer Satisfaction), 9.3 (Management Review), 10.2 (Nonconformity and Corrective Action). Industry best practices for Voice of Customer (VOC) collection and Key Performance Indicators (KPIs).",
  "clauseAlignment": "Directly addresses ISO 9001:2015 clause 9.1.2 requirements by: a) Determining methods for obtaining and using customer satisfaction information (multiple data sources, analysis methods). b) Monitoring customer perceptions (surveys, feedback, complaints). c) Defining how the information is monitored, reviewed (frequency, trending, management review), and acted upon (action triggers, communication). Ensures evidence-based decision making and drives continual improvement."
